    ============================================================
    PRACTICAL 14 - SCHEDULING TASKS (CRON AND AT)
    ============================================================

    A. Cron recurring tasks
    Check cron service:
        systemctl status crond
    Enable it:
        sudo systemctl enable --now crond

    Edit your user's crontab:
        crontab -e

    Example: run a date command every minute and append output to a file:
        * * * * * date >> /home/USERNAME/cron-log.txt

    Replace USERNAME with your Linux username. Save and exit the editor.
    View jobs:
        crontab -l
    Remove all jobs for your user (careful):
        crontab -r

    Cron format:
        minute hour day-of-month month day-of-week command
        * * * * * means every minute.

    B. At one-time scheduling
    Install at:
        sudo dnf install -y at
    Enable service:
        sudo systemctl enable --now atd

    Schedule a one-time task:
        echo 'date >> /tmp/at-demo.txt' | at now + 2 minutes
    List jobs:
        atq
    Check output after the scheduled time:
        cat /tmp/at-demo.txt

    Remove a queued job:
        atrm JOB_NUMBER

